<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.660 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.660 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE MARCH 31, 2002</p>
<p>			     $12.516 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.660    Awarded At	=99.853     6.625</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.640    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.490    29 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.54 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Mar.02</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Mar.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 26.Mar.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.516 BLN USD		 CUSIP   9128272P6</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   31.737			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   644.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.625</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.100 BLN		     PRICE	 99.853</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.490-6.660 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.660</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD UP FROM 6.359 PCT AT AUCTION ON 26.FEB.97</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD HIGHEST SINCE 6.674 PCT AT AUCTION 26.JUN.96</p>
